// Pull request: #5643 feat: susp service priv esc and phantom hijack rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5643
// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious SC.EXE Config Change for Services Vulnerable to Phantom DLL Hijacking
// Sigma ID: 46fa22de-556f-4355-a8c2-463e1c6ce2b3
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-09-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects the use of SC.EXE to modify configurations of known services that have been abused by
//   threat actors for phantom DLL hijacking. Since, these services load the phantom DLLs, threat
//   actors may modify their configurations to load malicious DLLs instead at runtime.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://blog.fox-it.com/2025/09/01/three-lazarus-rats-coming-for-your-cheese/
//   - https://specterops.io/blog/2019/04/18/lateral-movement-scm-and-dll-hijacking-primer/
//   - https://github.com/rapid7/metasploit-framework/blob/45bc95a87634b2e9871846447e2cfee5df7e14db/modules/exploits/windows/local/ikeext_service.rb
//   - https://github.com/djhohnstein/TSMSISrv_poc
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e518ed5635f1cb438da9c24198ce30d826249df3/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sc_service_config_change_for_phantom_dll_hijacking.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\SC.EXE" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "SC.EXE") and ProcessCommandLine contains "config" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "SessionEnv" or ProcessCommandLine contains "IKEEXT")
